nclude the full contents of the ecc-code-reviewer.md file. Let me read that file first.\n\nSteps:\n1. Read .claude/agents/ecc-code-reviewer.md (and ecc-planner.md if I decide to re-run planner — but the planner just completed; its output is in the retry context. I think re-running planner is unnecessary and wasteful; the retry context says \"build on the previous partial progress. Don't redo already-committed work.\").\n\nHmm, but the loop contract says \"must spawn and run planner + code-reviewer every loop — must not skip delegation.\" The planner was just run (its report is in the retry context) and returned COMPLETE. The review phase was interrupted. So for the remainder of this loop, spawn the code-reviewer to get the verdict. If the verdict is APPROVE → marker → commit → push → done.\n\n2. First quickly check the working tree state with git status (is it OK for the orchestrator to run read-only git status? The orchestrator can coordinate and verify results — yes, verification via read-only commands is fine).\n\nLet me do this: read the reviewer agent file + git status in parallel.\n","signature":"03f736172686421095053d4282a94504"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72843,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b0d085c-794f-4a13-b382-caa8d1cb5a12","uuid":"c1291725-3f00-473a-b7f1-afd7ac9f5118","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:01:03.024Z"}
