est's \"AC 2\" label covers packageManager/engines, which is part of story AC1). It's just a label mismatch, not a coverage gap. Skip — style level.\n\nEverything passes. Verdict: APPROVE, zero findings. Should I note the label nitpick as LOW? The task says to only flag issues with 80%+ confidence. Mislabeling is real but purely a cosmetic issue, and doesn't affect the acceptance criteria. Should I include it as one LOW (just a note) or zero? The instructions say \"zero findings is acceptable and expected.\" Mislabeling is a genuine observation but minor; to keep the review honest and actionable, I'll report it as LOW (note). Actually, the pre-report gate: can I cite the exact lines? Yes (test/package.test.cjs:19). Failure mode: none — it's just a label. \"Is the severity defensible?\" LOW, note. I'll include it as a LOW note.\n","signature":"657188dcc5284f01a873acf58e8c99ee"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26499,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ee265d391772b3f","session_id":"6b0d085c-794f-4a13-b382-caa8d1cb5a12","uuid":"3f1f0cf7-1c1a-4dfd-baec-926cf369ab15","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:07:32.406Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"code-reviewer: final verdict STORY-setup-001a"}
