t test/package.test.cjs`: **4/4 pass, 0 fail, exit 0.**\n\n## Supporting Files\n\n- `package-lock.json`: `lockfileVersion: 3` (sane), root entry mirrors `devDependencies.turbo: ^2.5.0`, and the `node_modules/turbo` entry at `2.10.11` satisfies `^2.5.0` — consistent.\n- `.gitignore`: `node_modules/` correctly appended.\n- No secrets, no stray fields in `package.json`; JSON validity of both `package.json` and `package-lock.json` confirmed via parse.\n- Git health: branch `iotahub/phase-1`; story files committed and clean; only uncommitted/untracked items are orchestrator housekeeping (`.story-updates/`, `.ralph/`, `ralph.log`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph-summary.txt`, `.last-branch`), explicitly out of story scope per instructions.\n\n## Findings\n\n### LOW\n\n```\n[LOW] Test subtest labels don't line up with story AC numbering\nFile: test/package.test.cjs:19, test/package.test.cjs:30\nIssue: The subtest at line 19 is labeled \"AC 2: pinned npm and Node 22 engines\"\nbut packageManager/engines belong to story AC 1, while the subtest at line 30,\nlabeled \"AC 3\", covers story AC 2 (turbo + scripts). Coverage is complete and\ncorrect — only the labels are offset by one.\nFix (optional): Relabel subtests to match the story's AC numbers (e.g.\n\"AC 1a: identity and workspaces\", \"AC 1b: npm pin and Node 22 engines\",\n\"AC 2: turbo 2.x and turbo-run scripts\").\n```\n\nNo CRITICAL, HIGH, or MEDIUM issues found. No hardcoded credentials, no injection/unsanitized-input surface (no runtime logic in this story), no dead code, and the file sizes are minimal.\n\n## Review Summary\n\n| Severity | Count | Status |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| CRITICAL | 0     | pass   |\n| HIGH     | 0     | pass   |\n| MEDIUM   | 0     | pass   |\n| LOW      | 1     | note   |\n\nVerdict: APPROVE","usage":{"total_tokens":26499,"tool_uses":8,"duration_ms":223814},"uuid":"7584db6a-510a-484b-9b33-ac0141e59fde","session_id":"6b0d085c-794f-4a13-b382-caa8d1cb5a12"}
